MODULE evaluate_button
FORMAT Pseudocode.
PURPOSE restore a declared checkpoint, evaluate it once, and export aligned predictions
PAPER Section 5.1.3; Eqs. (34)-(37)
DEPENDENCIES train_evaluate_functions.pseudo; lib/utils_CUROP.pseudo; models/Net_0207.pseudo

INPUT CONTRACT
    Invocation supplies config_filename and checkpoint_path explicitly.
    Evaluation loads the checkpoint selected by validation.
    Artifact manifest identifies station order, RDS, residual shares, feature schema and scaler.
    Record the configured random seed.
    Initialize model structure before restoring checkpoint parameters.

PROCEDURE read_cfg_file(filename,invocation=ABSENT)
    INPUT filename; optional normalized checkpoint-evaluation invocation.
    PARAMETERS config schema and checkpoint/evaluation settings.
    OUTPUT cfg with ComponentContext, validation report and provenance.
    IF invocation is ABSENT:
        invocation <- {entrypoint:checkpoint_evaluation,mode:evaluate,dry_specification_validation:false}.
    END IF
    cfg,provenance <- config.load_configuration(filename,invocation.get('project_root',ABSENT),invocation).
    cfg.provenance <- provenance.
    RETURN cfg.
END PROCEDURE

CLASS StepLR2
    Preserve the legacy public scheduler name for source-file completeness.
    This helper is not invoked by a read-only evaluation run.
    Its normative algorithm is train_evaluate_functions.StepLR2.

PROCEDURE StepLR2.__init__(optimizer,milestones,gamma=0.1,last_epoch=-1,min_lr=2.0e-6)
    INPUT optimizer.
    PARAMETERS milestones, gamma=0.1, last_epoch=-1, min_lr=2.0e-6.
    OUTPUT initialized scheduler with restored epoch and base group rates.
        Validate optimizer groups, nonnegative milestones and allowed rate ranges.
        Store the provided last_epoch.
        Delegate state construction to the common StepLR2 contract.
        Record scheduling convention and base group rates in state.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE StepLR2.get_lr()
    INPUT current object state.
    PARAMETERS None.
    OUTPUT one proposed learning rate per optimizer parameter group.
        Read proposed rates at the current state without advancing an epoch.
        Clamp each proposed group rate below by min_lr.
        RETURN one rate per optimizer group.
END PROCEDURE
END CLASS

PROCEDURE init_weights(module)
    INPUT module.
    PARAMETERS None.
    OUTPUT updated state of eligible newly constructed layers.
    Retain this legacy initialization helper for callers constructing a NEW model.
    Run this initialization before loading the evaluation checkpoint.
    IF module explicitly exposes a trainable dense Linear weight:
        Initialize weight with a declared Xavier-uniform gain.
        Initialize bias using the configured bias policy.
    ELSE IF module is a supported graph convolution:
        Invoke its own reset_parameters contract covering every projection and attention term.
    ELSE:
        Preserve parameters and allow the module's own constructor contract to govern them.
    Record the initialization scheme in a new training run's manifest.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE toDevice(datalist,device)
    INPUT datalist.
    PARAMETERS device.
    OUTPUT structured list with numeric values transferred to device.
    Preserve the legacy list interface but return a new container where practical.
    FOR each element in datalist:
        IF tensor: move to device preserving integer indices and floating dtype.
        IF sparse tensor: move indices/values while preserving sparsity and shape.
        IF BatchBundle/SimpleBatch: invoke its recursive transfer contract.
        IF list/tuple/mapping: recursively transfer tensor leaves.
        IF timestamp, path, sample ID or immutable metadata: preserve on host.
        IF unsupported mutable object: fail with the precise element path.
    END FOR
    REQUIRE graph indices and model operands share the target device.
    RETURN transferred data without assigning device semantics to plain Python strings.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE main(args)
    INPUT checkpoint-evaluation invocation args.
    PARAMETERS cfg.evaluation policies and declared device/output locations.
    OUTPUT EvaluationResult and prediction export manifest.
    PHASE 1: Read the checkpoint and its transforms.
    cfg <- read_cfg_file(args.config_filename,invocation=args).
    checkpoint_path <- args.checkpoint_path when supplied, otherwise cfg.model.save_path.
    REQUIRE checkpoint_path and its provenance manifest both exist.
    requested_split <- args.requested_split when supplied, otherwise cfg.evaluation.requested_split.
    REQUIRE requested_split in {train,val,test}.
    log_dir <- _get_log_dir(cfg,purpose='evaluation',resume_run_id=ABSENT).
    logger <- utils.get_logger(log_dir,'evaluate_button','info.log',cfg.log_level,write_to_file=true).
    Record start timestamp, pseudocode edition ID and invocation parameters.
    Seed stochastic libraries only when cfg.seed is supplied; record deterministic policy.
    device <- selected available device according to an explicit CPU/GPU fallback policy.
    Log the selected device.
    state <- LOAD_CHECKPOINT_WITH_MANIFEST(checkpoint_path,device).
    checkpoint_manifest <- state.manifest.
    saved_scaler <- READ_VERIFIED_ARTIFACT(checkpoint_manifest.od_scaler_reference).
    checkpoint_scaler <- utils.StandardScaler(saved_scaler.mean,saved_scaler.raw_std,
        transform_manifest=saved_scaler.transform_manifest).
    Verify its saved transform_id, axes,effective scale and fit metadata without recomputing statistics.
    IF frequency normalization was used by the checkpoint:
        saved_frequency_scaler <- READ_VERIFIED_ARTIFACT(checkpoint_manifest.frequency_scaler_reference).
        checkpoint_frequency_scaler <- utils.StandardScaler(saved_frequency_scaler.mean,
            saved_frequency_scaler.raw_std,transform_manifest=saved_frequency_scaler.transform_manifest).
    ELSE:
        checkpoint_frequency_scaler <- ABSENT.
    END IF
    component_context <- merge cfg.resolved_component_context, cfg.artifacts and the validated checkpoint manifest.
    Reject a changed model-component profile or conflicting immutable IDs before loading data.
    component_context.checkpoint_manifest <- checkpoint_manifest.
    component_context.checkpoint_transform_id <- checkpoint_scaler.transform_id.
    num_nodes <- cfg.model.num_nodes.
    N <- num_nodes.
    seq_len <- cfg.model.seq_len.
    horizon <- cfg.model.horizon.
    output_dim <- cfg.model.output_dim.
    REQUIRE these agree with the checkpoint manifest; validate dataset agreement after loading.
    flags <- normalize component switches from the legacy and current config schemas.
    Reject conflicting legacy/current names.
    PHASE 2: Build the graph and restore the requested data split.
    graph <- utils.BUILD_GRAPH_BUNDLE(cfg,cfg.artifacts,device).
    edge_index <- graph.edge_index; edge_attr <- graph.edge_attr.
    dataset <- utils.load_dataset(dataset_dir=cfg.data.dataset_dir,
        batch_size=cfg.data.batch_size, test_batch_size=cfg.data.test_batch_size,
        scaler_axis=checkpoint_scaler.axes, options=cfg.data with training_mode=false,
        fit_scaler=false, scaler=checkpoint_scaler, frequency_scaler=checkpoint_frequency_scaler,
        phases=[requested_split], component_context=component_context).
    REQUIRE the frozen training-fitted scaler.
    Check dataset includes every expected target sample and alignment identifier.
    Bind verified immutable artifact references under cfg.artifacts.
    Bind cfg.artifacts.od_scaler to utils.StandardScaler_Torch(checkpoint_scaler.mean,
        checkpoint_scaler.raw_std,device,transform_manifest=checkpoint_scaler.transform_manifest).
    Bind the restored frequency scaler and set cfg.initialization_mode=evaluate_checkpoint.
    PHASE 3: Construct and restore the model.
    model <- Net_0207(cfg,logger) using the checkpoint architecture and registered submodule contracts.
    Constructor initialization must not refit scalers, recalibrate zeta or reset restored utility coefficients.
    Move model once to selected device.
    Validate architecture signature before attempting parameter assignment.
    Check state station count, RDS count, graph relation count and encoder dimensions.
    REQUIRE coefficient and encoder parameters included in the main checkpoint.
    Compare checkpoint keys to constructed model keys.
    IF names/shapes disagree:
        Allow only an explicit, versioned migration with a documented key mapping.
        Report missing/unexpected/mismatched keys and stop if not fully explained.
    Load parameter state strictly after any approved migration.
    Verify checkpoint auxiliary/scaler references exist and match hashes.
    Switch model to evaluation mode and disable optimizer updates.
    PHASE 4: Evaluate once and export matching arrays.
    result <- evaluate(model=model, dataset=dataset, dataset_type=requested_split,
        num_nodes=num_nodes, edge_index=edge_index, edge_attr=edge_attr, device=device,
        seq_Len=seq_len, horizon=horizon, output_dim=output_dim,
        four_step_method_included=flags.four_step_method_included,
        history_distribution_included=flags.history_distribution_included,
        traffic_assignment_included=flags.traffic_assignment_included,
        depart_freq_included=flags.depart_freq_included, logger=logger,
        cfg=cfg, return_predictions=true).
    Assert result.sample_count = dataset.expected_counts[requested_split].
    Persist result.y_evaluated as test_pred.npy (or split-specific equivalent).
    Persist result.y_truth as test_true.npy in exactly the same sample order.
    Optionally persist result.y_raw as test_pred_raw.npy with a distinct label.
    Persist valid_mask, sample_ids, forecast origins and per-horizon timestamps.
    Persist per-horizon and mean metrics in machine-readable and human-readable forms.
    Persist prediction export manifest with units, output policy and source artifact IDs.
    IF optional path/section outputs exist, export their explicit OD/path/section indexes.
    Verify export row counts, shapes and content hashes before marking run complete.
    Emit paths and concise metrics using the same arrays just saved.
    Record elapsed time and evaluation completion status.
    RETURN EvaluationResult and artifact manifest.
END PROCEDURE

PROCEDURE LOAD_CHECKPOINT_WITH_MANIFEST(path,device)
    INPUT path.
    PARAMETERS device.
    OUTPUT checkpoint manifest, model state and immutable artifact references.
    REQUIRE the checkpoint is a trusted local artifact or a safe data-only format.
    Read external manifest before allocating large arrays.
    Verify content hash, schema version and model family.
    Load tensors using an explicit device map, permitting CPU-only evaluation.
    Distinguish bare legacy parameter dictionaries from full checkpoint bundles.
    IF bare legacy parameters:
        REQUIRE the supplied artifact manifest.
    IF training bundle:
        Extract model_state and immutable artifact references.
        Ignore optimizer/scheduler state during read-only evaluation.
    Validate every required parameter has finite values and expected dtype/shape.
    RETURN normalized checkpoint record with manifest, model_state and immutable artifact references.
END PROCEDURE

SCRIPT ENTRY
    Parse the explicit configuration/checkpoint arguments.
    Invoke main exactly once when this module is used as the entry point.
    Importing equivalent future modules must not seed RNGs, read files or start evaluation.
